<p>Each part of that background helps in a different way. Adjusting for insurers shows how a carrier estimate gets built and where it tends to come up short. Appraisal and umpire work shows how disputed amounts are settled. Construction experience helps answer the practical question underneath every claim: what does this repair really involve? Joseph also writes and reviews the guides on this site.</p>
